  "body": "Stacked on #3062 (merge #3062 first).\n\nThis PR is partial work on #3035. It does the warning part only.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `camcraft_sim::verify::Warning` has a new variant, `StrategyFallback { at, areas }`.\n  - It is advisory. `blocks_post` is false.\n  - `at` is the first cutting move. `areas` is the number of areas that the Offset rings cut in place of the Adaptive plan.\n- Generate (`operation/generate.rs`) counts the fallback notes and adds the warning when the count is more than zero.\n  - The op now reports `warnings` > 0 in MCP `get_job` and `generate`.\n  - MCP `verify` lists the finding as `strategy_fallback` with `blocks_post: false`.\n  - The UI folds the warning on its own key (225).\n- `machining2d::RINGS_FALLBACK` holds the note tail `\" - Offset rings cut \"`. The 2D door (`pocket_hsm`) and the 3D ladder (`machining3d::hsm::rings_tag`) both use it. `machining2d::rings_fallbacks` counts the notes by it. The note text does not change.\n- The rest pass and the offset shells are not counted. Their Offset rings are by design, not a fallback.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe planner wrote each fallback to Offset rings only into the path notes. The op status stayed `ok` with `warnings=0`. In the QA run, 14 levels fell back and nothing showed it except the notes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins:\n  - `app strategy_fallback::an_adaptive_fallback_to_offset_rings_is_a_warning` (new). Before the fix it failed: `one fallback warning: []`, left 0, right 1.\n  - `motion lib machining3d::hsm::fallback_tests::a_refused_level_counts_as_one_rings_fallback` (new).\n- Mutations:\n  - `generate.rs` from upstream/main (no guard): the app pin is red. Restored: green.\n  - `rings_fallbacks` that matches nothing: the motion pin is red. Restored: green.\n- Expected changes: these suites pinned \"verifies clean\" as zero warnings on fixtures that already fall back to rings. Each now allows only the fallback warning, and only when the notes name a fallback:\n  - `adaptive_pinch`\n  - `adaptive_zero_margin_island` (the MCP `findings` check skips `strategy_fallback` only)\n  - `climb_direction`\n  - `shoulder_adaptive`\n- Historical quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 313 steps, zero failures. Sim, motion, app and UI pass. The UI library passes. Duration: 65.6 minutes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Warning display screenshots\n\nThe images show the real operation properties page for the Milling-test channel fixture.\nThe capture uses the same parameters as `an_adaptive_fallback_to_offset_rings_is_a_warning`.\nBefore omits only the new advisory from the generated cache to reproduce the previous display.\nAfter uses the exact generated cache. The moves and path notes are the same.\nThe temporary capture assertions passed. No capture code or images are on this PR branch.\n\nBefore: `OK · 73 moves`.\n\n![Warning display before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/41f8ad4764cce2abb6eb9905576b14fb1d84eeb7/3108/warning-before.png)\n\nAfter: `OK · 73 moves · 1 warning`, with the expanded Adaptive fallback advisory.\n\n![Warning display after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/41f8ad4764cce2abb6eb9905576b14fb1d84eeb7/3108/warning-after.png)\n\n## Author review fixes\n\nHead: `9562dd2adc3f0cb36a90d7103fb1eb6c5a84f039`.\n\nThe first full heavy run found six stale warning assertions. The fixes change tests only.\nEach guard requires the warning count to match the fallback notes.\nEach guard accepts only `StrategyFallback`, with the same area count and `blocks_post: false`.\nThe geometry checks and configured known-failure assertions remain unchanged.\n\nThe six pins are:\n\n- `adaptive_pinch::the_users_part_with_default_adaptive_keeps_the_cutter_off_it`\n- `pick_agnostic::a_face_with_an_island_and_its_rim_loop_cut_the_same_bytes_around_the_boss_full`\n- `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`\n- `shoulder_adaptive::containment_outside_clears_past_the_edge_never_the_recess`\n- `shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`\n- `whole_model_pocket::a_whole_part_adaptive_at_the_default_load_keeps_the_full_tool_radius_off_the_part`\n\nMutation check: remove the warning insertion from `generate.rs`.\nAll six pins fail at the warning guard: zero actual warnings, one expected warning.\nRestore the source byte for byte: the targeted heavy gate passes nine steps.\nThe two affected known-failure tests reach their original configured failure reasons.\nThe selector also includes two unchanged lead-approach known-failure checks.\n\n## Final verification\n\nVerified head: `19a736d203de3ff590de1caea27a74e951966b6c`.\nThe head is unchanged. This review request required verification only.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: **PASS**, 241 steps, zero gate failures, 59.2 minutes.\n  Base at plan creation: `9e8e2135cd4cc580ccb91dfd2ec504c16c9950c7`.\n  The gate reached all motion and app heavy targets.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: **PASS**, 343 steps, zero failures, no retries, 53.1 minutes.\n  Base at plan creation: `0aad72f8825de7a3871b42eea05dbe98a68788a6`.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: **PASS**.\n\nAnother session advanced the shared `upstream/main` reference between the gate starts.\nEach gate selected its tests from the base recorded above. The tested head did not change.\nThe compile cache stalled before the heavy gate started. The completed runs used the cache disabled.\n\n| Heavy lane | Ordinary tests passed | Configured known-failure tests with expected reasons | Unexpected failures |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Motion | 59 | 2 | 0 |\n| App | 44 | 2 | 0 |\n\nThe motion known-failure checks reach their configured stock-ring reasons (#1950).\nThe app known-failure checks reach their configured bore fallback (#1950) and shoulder clearance (#2849) reasons.\nAll six warning guards listed above ran in the full heavy gate.\nNo configured known-failure check failed for a different reason.\n\n| Quick lane | Tests passed | Failed | Ignored |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Sim | 467 | 0 | 1 |\n| Motion | 1163 | 0 | 58 |\n| App | 1757 | 0 | 27 |\n| UI | 1440 | 0 | 7 |\n\nThe UI library passed 1409 tests. The UI operations suite passed 31 tests.\nThe worktree stayed clean. No source change, new pin, or mutation was needed for this verification request.\nNo golden, screenshot, log, or review artifact is on this PR branch.\n\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes. The posted G-code does not change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The QA part of #3035 (the mould core STL on len) did not run.\n- Two parts of #3035 stay open:\n  - the run time of Rough12, Rest6 and Waterline6 (5 to 13 min, or more);\n  - a long generate that blocks every other MCP call, with no cancel tool.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3062: the same function (`fold_warnings_located`, `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`). This PR is stacked on it.\n- #3080 and #2714 touch `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`, different variants and arms. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3103, #3033 and #2836 touch `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`, other functions. #2836 adds `UndercutLift` on key 222; this PR uses 225.\n- Many open PRs touch `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`. This PR adds 7 lines after the drill-size law.\n\nEffort: max (this part is smaller; the rest of #3035 stays at its label).\n\nChangelog: An Adaptive operation that falls back to Offset rings now shows a warning with the number of areas, not only a note; the post is not held.\n\nRefs #3035\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
